  "notes": [
    "Rust 2021 Cargo workspace (tokio 1 async, reqwest 0.12 rustls-tls, serde 1, thiserror 2, anyhow 1) with 10 member crates; no database; state lives in ~/.mehh/agent JSON files.",
    "crates/mehh-ai/src/oauth.rs:12-35 stores OAuth access/refresh tokens and API keys in ~/.mehh/agent/auth.json; PKCE verifier generated from two UUIDv4 byte strings (lines 72-84); loopback callback listener and device-code flow are network trust boundaries.",
    "crates/mehh-coding-agent/src/permissions.rs:39-117 loads global user rules then workspace rules only when trusted; repo-local AlwaysAllow rules are filtered out so a project cannot grant itself access; path globs matched against canonicalized paths (lines 55-75) to stop ../ and symlink bypass.",
    "crates/mehh-tools/src/core/shell.rs:31-44 parses timeout from model-supplied tool params and clamps to 600s; kill_process_tree (lines 78-111) shells out to taskkill/kill via PID; UTF8 PowerShell exit-suffix logic (lines 23-26) can rewrite failure exits.",
    "Tool inputs originate from model output (untrusted) and cross into shell execution, file read/write/edit, and file_mutation_queue; permissions.rs and trust.rs are the authorization gates.",
    "crates/mehh-mcp/src/oauth.rs and transport.rs are client-side OAuth/transport boundaries; mehh-codemode/src/sandbox.rs and mehh-sandbox/src/lib.rs isolate dynamic tool code execution.",
    "Concurrency: tokio tasks in agent_loop/lead_worker/subagent* share session state; file_mutation_queue serializes writes; cancellation tokens gate long-running shell commands.",
    "docs/handoff/gemini-coding-agent-gaps/raw/** are documentation snapshots of crates sources; they are read-only reference copies, not compiled production code.",
    "Working tree has uncommitted modifications across many crates source files; state hashes were captured at run init and hash-verify will fail closed if these change mid-run."
